f70307671542f228874af64585d4.png" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334201 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535154 true] [17592186334201 1111 #uuid "5983fc8b-57bb-531d-bc87-c33bb1bb5cb9" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334202 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055663/assets/2f966ea4bc8d2257a9082347c1bf774cbb40f0c2b5561a0d051fe088bdab43d2.png" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334202 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535154 true] [17592186334202 1111 #uuid "a1033193-e2a8-5234-8c41-558d547c0871" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334203 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334204 13194139535154 true] [17592186334203 1089 "q-49238" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334203 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535154 true] [17592186334203 1100 "The rate, in degrees Farhenheit per month, at which the average midday temperature in New York City varies, does so according to the function $R(t)={t}^{3}+3,$ where $t$ is the number of months since the measurements began. Estimate the total increase in air temperature over the first three months using the trapezoidal rule with $3$ trapezoids of equal height." 13194139535154 true] [17592186334203 1113 #uuid "5be4a2da-fb76-54b9-819f-4f8cf046d700" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334203 1145 "In this context, the area $A$ under the curve $y=R(t)$ over the interval $[0,3]$ represents the total increase in air temperature over the first three months.\n\nThe general formula for the trapezoidal rule states that\n\n$$\nA≈\\frac{1}{2}[R(a)+2(R({t}_{1})+R({t}_{2})+⋯+R({t}_{n-1}))+R(b)]Δt,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of trapezoids and $Δt=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ is the step size.\n\nHere, we have the following values:\n\n- The number of trapezoids is $n=3.$\n\n- The corresponding interval is $[0,3],$ so we have $a=0$ and $b=3.$\n\n- The step size is given by\n\n$$\nΔt=\\frac{b-a}{n}=\\frac{3-0}{3}=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above values, the general formula becomes\n\n$$\nA≈\\frac{1}{2}[R(0)+2(R(1)+R(2))+R(3)]\\cdot 1.\n$$\n\nTo identify the function values, we now set up a table with the values of $t$ and $R(t):$\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $R(t)$ | $3$ | $4$ | $11$ | $30$ |\n\nSubstituting the appropriate numbers into the above expression gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈\\frac{1}{2}[3+2(4+11)+30]\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{63}{2} \\\\  & =31.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total air temperature increase is approximately ${31.5}^{∘}\\,\\text{F}.$" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334205 13194139535154 true] [17592186334204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334206 13194139535154 true] [17592186334204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334207 13194139535154 true] [17592186334204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334208 13194139535154 true] [17592186334204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334209 13194139535154 true] [17592186334204 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535154 true] [17592186334204 1041 "selection" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334204 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334205 13194139535154 true] [17592186334204 1110 #uuid "d1854635-102f-5870-9d42-7884e785e958" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334205 1034 "{31.5}^{∘}\\,\\text{F}" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334205 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535154 true] [17592186334205 1111 #uuid "c60bea12-49c3-527f-81d8-6db076320f40" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334206 1034 "{50}^{∘}\\,\\text{F}" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334206 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535154 true] [17592186334206 1111 #uuid "1c5425f2-376b-56e1-995a-7c03bdb8e43d" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334207 1034 "{24.5}^{∘}\\,\\text{F}" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334207 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535154 true] [17592186334207 1111 #uuid "4cb94d95-ba36-571a-96c2-77c21d2006a8" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334208 1034 "{45}^{∘}\\,\\text{F}" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334208 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535154 true] [17592186334208 1111 #uuid "e6358295-4e32-51f4-a961-883434cecb15" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334209 1034 "{48.5}^{∘}\\,\\text{F}" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334209 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535154 true] [17592186334209 1111 #uuid "cae62c33-68ab-5837-8372-1ce39e78c87e" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334210 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334211 13194139535154 true] [17592186334210 1089 "q-51076" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334210 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535154 true] [17592186334210 1100 "The following table shows the rate $r(t),$ in centimeters per hour, at which rain is falling during a two-hour period of a certain day.\n\n| $t\\,\\text{(hours)}$ | $0$ | $0.5$ | $1$ | $1.5$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $r\\,\\text{(centimeters/hour)}$ | $3$ | $4$ | $3$ | $3$ | $1$ |\n\nApproximate the total amount of rainfall during this period using the trapezoidal rule with $4$ trapezoids of equal height." 13194139535154 true] [17592186334210 1113 #uuid "ab3c0204-d78f-5315-ac2e-2155f33a9b69" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334210 1145 "In this context, the area $A$ under the curve $y=r(t)$ over the interval $[0,2]$ represents the total amount of rainfall during the two-hour period.\n\nThe general formula for the trapezoidal rule states that\n\n$$\nA≈\\frac{1}{2}[r(a)+2(r({t}_{1})+r({t}_{2})+⋯+r({t}_{n-1}))+r(b)]Δt,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of trapezoids and $Δt=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ is the step size.\n\nHere, we have the following values:\n\n- The number of trapezoids is $n=4.$\n\n- The corresponding interval is $[0,2],$ so we have $a=0$ and $b=2.$\n\n- The step size is given by\n\n$$\nΔt=\\frac{b-a}{n}=\\frac{2-0}{4}=0.5.\n$$\n\nUsing the above values, the general formula becomes\n\n$$\nA≈\\frac{1}{2}[r(0)+2(r(0.5)+r(1)+r(1.5))+r(2)]\\cdot 0.5.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the appropriate numbers from the given table in the above expression gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈\\frac{1}{2}[3+2(4+3+3)+1]\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.25(24) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, approximately $6\\,\\text{cm}$ of rain fell during the given two-hour period." 13194139535154 true] [17592186334211 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334212 13194139535154 true] [17592186334211 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334213 13194139535154 true] [17592186334211 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334214 13194139535154 true] [17592186334211 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334215 13194139535154 true] [17592186334211 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334216 13194139535154 true] [17592186334211 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535154 true] [17592186334211 1041 "selection" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334211 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334212 13194139535154 true] [17592186334211 1110 #uuid "2bb03d1f-a98f-5a87-8b3a-32048ad183fa" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334212 1034 "6\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334212 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535154 true] [17592186334212 1111 #uuid "6a0915ac-d0c5-52e9-be1d-358ab643ad99" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334213 1034 "4\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334213 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535154 true] [17592186334213 1111 #uuid "bd6434dd-80e9-5c65-a561-cf3fa659e3f1" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334214 1034 "7\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334214 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535154 true] [17592186334214 1111 #uuid "688bbd9f-757a-5f14-881d-524639cf9645" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334215 1034 "5\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334215 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535154 true] [17592186334215 1111 #uuid "57738d1c-a2ee-53d0-9e42-f41f692e8e96" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334216 1034 "8\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334216 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535154 true] [17592186334216 1111 #uuid "f5bdc49b-d082-594b-8de1-018b6944b54a" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334217 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334218 13194139535154 true] [17592186334217 1089 "q-51077" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334217 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535154 true] [17592186334217 1100 "The following table shows the speed $V(t),$ in miles per hour, at which an airplane flies at certain times since its $2$-hour journey began.\n\n| $t\\,(\\text{hours})$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $V\\,(\\text{miles/hour})$ | $150$ | $250$ | $200$ |\n\nApproximate the total distance traveled by the plane using the trapezoidal rule with $2$ trapezoids of equal height.\n\n*Hint: The distance traveled is given by the area under the speed-time graph.*" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334217 1113 #uuid "f29b6971-06ec-5eb0-87ec-6449e746727e" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334217 1145 "In this context, the area $A$ under the curve $y=V(t)$ over the interval $[0,2]$ represents the total distance traveled by the plane.\n\nThe general formula for the trapezoidal rule states that\n\n$$\nA≈\\frac{1}{2}[V(a)+2(V({t}_{1})+V({t}_{2})+⋯+V({t}_{n-1}))+V(b)]Δt,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of trapezoids and $Δt=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ is the step size.\n\nHere, we have the following values:\n\n- The number of trapezoids is $n=2.$\n\n- The corresponding interval is $[0,2],$ so we have $a=0$ and $b=2.$\n\n- The step size is given by\n\n$$\nΔt=\\frac{b-a}{n}=\\frac{2-0}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above values, the general formula becomes\n\n$$\nA≈\\frac{1}{2}[V(0)+2V(1)+V(2)]\\cdot 1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the appropriate numbers from the given table into the above expression gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈\\frac{1}{2}[150+2(250)+200]\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{850}{2} \\\\  & =425.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total distance traveled by the plane is approximately $425$ miles." 13194139535154 true] [17592186334218 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334219 13194139535154 true] [17592186334218 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334220 13194139535154 true] [17592186334218 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334221 13194139535154 true] [17592186334218 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334222 13194139535154 true] [17592186334218 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334223 13194139535154 true] [17592186334218 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535154 true] [17592186334218 1041 "selection" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334218 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334219 13194139535154 true] [17592186334218 1110 #uuid "3752c1ac-9857-5e9b-ae75-a35234cb2425" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334219 1034 "$425$ miles" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334219 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535154 true] [17592186334219 1111 #uuid "1e490f31-0082-5670-a54b-3575e1b7d4f1" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334220 1034 "$370$ miles" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334220 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535154 true] [17592186334220 1111 #uuid "f13f3974-b92f-52b1-a187-2ec78a10997c" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334221 1034 "$390$ miles" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334221 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535154 true] [17592186334221 1111 #uuid "7db1798e-9d66-5d90-8428-15207558c52f" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334222 1034 "$480$ miles" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334222 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535154 true] [17592186334222 1111 #uuid "5795d60e-135e-53f7-9888-46c421db4e61" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334223 1034 "$300$ miles" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334223 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535154 true] [17592186334223 1111 #uuid "1ca341f0-a694-5e2a-832e-c0fe3dea3137" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334224 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334225 13194139535154 true] [17592186334224 1089 "q-85636" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334224 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535154 true] [17592186334224 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055663/assets/89426d77a95ffb1a4780484ed1e1ad0531ccd1c4022419ef2c573a08922bf7eb.png)\n\nEstimate the area under the curve $y=4-{x}^{2}$ over the interval $[-1,2]$ using the trapezoidal rule with $3$ trapezoids of equal height.\n\n*Note: figure not drawn to scale.*" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334224 1113 #uuid "47f34064-59b1-5054-b709-399abe1fd2c4" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334224 1145 "Let $f(x)=4-{x}^{2}$ and let $A$ denote the required area. The general formula for the trapezoidal rule states that\n\n$$\nA≈\\frac{1}{2}[f(a)+2(f({x}_{1})+f({x}_{2})+…+f({x}_{n-1}))+f(b)]Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of trapezoids and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ is the step size.\n\nHere, we have the following values:\n\n- The number of trapezoids is $n=3.$\n\n- The corresponding interval is $[-1,2],$ so we have $a=-1$ and $b=2.$\n\n- The step size is given by\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{b-a}{n}=\\frac{2-(-1)}{3}=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above values, the general formula becomes\n\n$$\nA≈\\frac{1}{2}[f(-1)+2(f(0)+f(1))+f(2)]\\cdot 1.\n$$\n\nTo identify the function values, we now set up a table with the values of $x$ and $f(x):$\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $3$ | $4$ | $3$ | $0$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain the following approximation for our area:\n\n$$\nA≈\\frac{1}{2}[3+2(4+3)+0]\\cdot 1=\\frac{17}{2}\n$$\n\nBecause the function is *concave down* over the interval $[-1,2],$ the trapezoids lie under the function, and therefore approximation is an *underestimate* of the correct area." 13194139535154 true] [17592186334225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334226 13194139535154 true] [17592186334225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334227 13194139535154 true] [17592186334225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334228 13194139535154 true] [17592186334225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334229 13194139535154 true] [17592186334225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334230 13194139535154 true] [17592186334225 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535154 true] [17592186334225 1041 "selection" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334225 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334230 13194139535154 true] [17592186334225 1110 #uuid "f5dbbb38-3a0a-5459-b671-64510feb9786" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334226 1034 "\\frac{25}{4}" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334226 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535154 true] [17592186334226 1111 #uuid "9521d834-3f19-52a8-998d-a0bd8e17bac5" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334227 1034 "10" 13194139535154 true] [17592186334227 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535154 true] [17592186334227 1111 #uuid "48fa0f73-9ace-525f-a614-4249c2be74ac" 13194139535154 true] [1759218